# GPU landscape

**Trends**

---

## Stagnating FP64

- Hopper -> Blackwell *decreased* FP64 performance
    - 33 TFLOPS -> 30 TFLOPS
    - rebalancing FLOPS - MEMOPS
    - replaced with non-IEEE emulation
- AMD GPUs still improving FP64 performance
    - MI300X: 81.7 TFLOPS

## Most FLOPs in a GPU is now in tensor cores

- Both AMD & Nvidia tensor hardware offer FLOPS twice that of regular OPs
- Tricky to use effectively
- Basically only GEMM
- But many libraries available

## GPU memory is (slowly) increasing

- CPU systems easily host 2TB+ per node
- RAM per GPU is **80GB** (Hopper 2022) up to **288GB** (Rubin 2026)
    - Typically 4-8 GPUs per node, so ~2TB per node (for 20x the price...)

