# OpenMP

## `omp target`

```{.c code-line-numbers="1,2,7"}
#pragma omp target teams distribute parallel for \
  map(to: x[0:n],y[0:n]) map(from: out[0:n])
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
  out[i] = a*x[i] + y[i];
}

// synchronous by default!
```

- `target` — offload the region to the device
- `teams distribute` — split loop across teams/blocks
- `parallel for` — split each team across threads
- `map(to: ...)` — copy to device before
- `map(from: ...)` — copy from device after

## `omp target data`

```{.c code-line-numbers="1,2,8"}
#pragma omp target data map(to: x[0:n],y[0:n]) map(from: out[0:n])
{
#pragma omp target teams distribute parallel do
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    out[i] = a*x[i] + y[i];
  }
  ... // other GPU operations
}
```

## What about Fortran?

